  _menuDescription: He can't bark, he'll growl even when he's happy
  _funFacts:
  - _fact: Wolf pups are born with bright blue eyes, which typically transition to
      a golden-yellow or amber color by the time they are 6 to 8 weeks old.
  - _fact: A wolf's howl can travel up to 10 miles in open terrain. Contrary to popular
      folklore, they don't howl at the moon; their howling is mostly to locate pack
      members, communicate with other packs, and defend territory.
  - _fact: 'Wolf''s fur consists of two layers: coarse outer hairs to repel water
      and a soft undercoat to insulate them against temperatures far below freezing.'
  - _fact: "When a wolf pack needs to make a decision about hunting or moving territories,
      they use body language and vocalizations to display preferences\u2014acting
      almost like they are \"voting\" on the group's next move."
